Q: Dynamic configuration from appsettings at runtime A: <blockquote>
<p>This throws an invalid cast exception, unfortunately.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Your code <code>builder.Configuration.GetRequiredSection(&quot;SoapService&quot;)</code> returns the <code>IConfigurationSection</code>. Please note that it is impossible to convert type <code>IConfigurationSection</code> to type <code>SoapService</code> by casting.</p>
<p>I suggest the followings to achieve your requirements mentioned in you question:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I would like to read the appsettings.json file from the host application builder,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Define the <code>SoapService</code> class as a POCO (Plain Old CLR Object). A sample is shown below::</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class SoapService
{
    public string SoapScheme { get; set; } = &quot;&quot;;
    public string SoapServiceHost { get; set; } = &quot;&quot;;
    public CustomerAccountManagerConfig CustomerAccountManager { get; set; } = new();
}

public class CustomerAccountManagerConfig
{
    public string Endpoint { get; set; } = &quot;&quot;;
    public string Username { get; set; } = &quot;&quot;;
    public string Password { get; set; } = &quot;&quot;;
    public int TimeoutSeconds { get; set; } = 0;
    public int MaxReceivedMessageSize { get; set; } = 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Create the instance of <code>SoapService</code> class and bind it to the <code>IConfigurationSection</code> as shown below:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var soap = new SoapService();
builder.Configuration.GetRequiredSection(&quot;SoapService&quot;).Bind(soap);
</code></pre>
<p>The values in the <code>SoapService</code> section of appsettings.json are set to the <code>SoapService</code> object through the properties of <code>SoapService</code> class.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>determine my logic (in this case, if a service is running), then replace the placeholder parts of the string,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Overwrite the values in the <code>SoapService</code> object through its properties as required. For example:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>soap.SoapServiceHost = &quot;hostingService&quot;;
soap.CustomerAccountManager.Endpoint = &quot;https://example.com.endpoint&quot;;
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>and finally give it back to the builder to pass along to what needs it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Resister the <code>SoapService</code> object to the D/I container so that it can be used anywhere in the ASP.NET app as shown below:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>builder.Services.AddSingleton(soap);
</code></pre>
